{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-fppf}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:28e3137721550c9f125bcc580d4c32969510387f2b4fc8f9ab2fac5de4a5408c", "source_text": "The fppf topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a74da991a640d84eb874a100fc38140f430bb9d54f27a2289082fa5f8ebcbb67", "unit_id": "tag:021L:title"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\`e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3373d69d1a771d1b240d3f94798edce7e161caf54de4b2de49dd8524c8dc1502", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0b45f583fef23d2d5f19019a1a64a6e95cd71374f490e8752c31523537179fa1", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme. We would like to define the fppf-topology<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>\nThe letters fppf stand for ``fid<ACCENT_0001>lement plat de pr<ACCENT_0002>sentation finie''.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001> on\nthe category of schemes over <MATH_0002>. According to our general principle\nwe first introduce the notion of an fppf-covering.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:824188f7268ecb6bf73443b4857db5a4c54c232e9ccb87068a196ef439cdcd13", "unit_id": "tag:021L:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{f_i : T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0004": "$f_i$", "MATH_0005": "$T = \\bigcup f_i(T_i)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-fppf-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:283f9dea2be6a5f99e7e729bc3db42e6c914a1813f97c1b0e20c1ac32623e25a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:84b4d1a6117da9744fba633fcd2069375c974cc575ef626b5ccd49f77cb23094", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. An <TEXTITOPEN_0001>fppf covering of <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family\nof morphisms <MATH_0003> of schemes\nsuch that each <MATH_0004> is flat, locally of finite presentation and such\nthat <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7c726cccf7137afaee215c41f44d86303257c74a19beb0ac3fc564bbace892de", "unit_id": "tag:021M:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic-fppf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:116b94852419c9381610e7881b81307f250ab6e955289803bf2b4344d9a89dbe", "source_text": "Any syntomic covering is an fppf covering, and a fortiori,\nany smooth, <ACCENT_0001>tale, or Zariski covering is an fppf covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e54a07aa3f14b9b56c948804c03ea2ce48effbeac31a35a8a6732606055a838b", "unit_id": "tag:021N:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-syntomic-locally-finite-presentation}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-syntomic-flat}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:18e430d7eebaf9dd8e803fc514a1ca2f5f61ace034f3593eab1239a6a003b015", "source_text": "This is clear from the definitions, the fact that a syntomic morphism\nis flat and locally of finite presentation, see\nMorphisms, Lemmas\n<REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>,\nand\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:166dae4a15be2c6e48351b32184ea9dcf45a7ed8f9e49f16d4fe2e472652bb58", "unit_id": "tag:021N:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-site}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3cb5dc25576ea169d8afeb80aff8b3e3f28492ea74162e5d9eeea299db8327bc", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNext, we show that this notion satisfies the conditions of\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fe60d7ff7dec91903335c151eda3e3489f64647b495bf10d622c43cc9afc0c89", "unit_id": "tag:021L:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{T' \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0010": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{T' \\times_T T_i \\to T'\\}_{i\\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fppf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e2cfe153eb45f4e05511defe14a0d0d67a3d5c22cf50aff12afe0aee9a4b79d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:76dce918e2cfbba4524f5d8bd7bba605d25eef06adb560651e41a99bf0b03721", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is an isomorphism then <MATH_0003>\nis an fppf covering of <MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> is an fppf covering and for each\n<MATH_0006> we have an fppf covering <MATH_0007>, then\n<MATH_0008> is an fppf covering.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0009> is an fppf covering\nand <MATH_0010> is a morphism of schemes then\n<MATH_0011> is an fppf covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:838b2f0b9e347da84d7253344d3b72eeb9d7d99e1ba98c3bdd4c1b7bf260b77f", "unit_id": "tag:021O:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-composition-flat}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-composition-finite-presentation}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-base-change-flat}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-base-change-finite-presentation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b6f7d38af6873964e1ccb4c9de6ebe3b579dee40f606f201d7e2944ba1e69f0d", "source_text": "The first assertion is clear.\nThe second follows as the composition of flat morphisms is flat\n(see Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>)\nand the composition of morphisms of finite presentation is\nof finite presentation\n(see Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nThe third follows as the base change of a flat morphism is flat\n(see Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0003>)\nand the base change of a morphism of finite presentation is\nof finite presentation\n(see Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0004>).\nMoreover, the base change of a surjective family of morphisms is surjective\n(proof omitted).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:173551c0a0b95ae7074c4190614830e13f09e09cc794e2fa2391188e035e5c02", "unit_id": "tag:021O:proof"}
